{"timestamp": 1779433256.0999238, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 10, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433268.6940322, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I just found Alice's body in electrical. My path this round was storage, then medbay, and finally electrical where I found her. \n\nWhile I was passing through medbay, I saw Frank there. Frank, did you see anyone else pass by or head towards electrical? I didn't see anyone else leaving the room when I got there, so the killer might have vented or slipped away just before I arrived. Let's hear everyone's locations\u2014who else was on the left side of the map?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433277.667445, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started the round in electrical. At tick 3, Alice walked into electrical from the cafeteria, and Frank was already in there with me. I left them both alive in electrical around tick 4 and headed to security. \n\nIn security, I saw Diana pass through from navigation to weapons around tick 6, so Diana is cleared for this. \n\nEve, your timeline confirms everything perfectly. If I left Frank and Alice alone in electrical, and then you saw Frank in medbay before finding Alice's body in electrical... Frank absolutely killed her right after I left and fled to medbay. We need to vote Frank!"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433286.349744, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I spent this whole round on the left side of the ship. I started in upper engine, went up to oxygen to do a task, and then came back down to upper engine. I haven't seen a single person the entire round. \n\nCharlie, your timeline and logic seem really solid, especially since Eve's sighting of Frank in medbay perfectly lines up with him leaving electrical after you did. It definitely looks bad for Frank. I want to hear what Frank has to say for himself before we officially lock in our votes, but right now I'm leaning heavily towards voting him. Let's see if Diana's testimony matches what you saw in security, Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433315.506361, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I get why it looks bad on paper, but Charlie is leaving out the key part: Alice was still alive when I left electrical. I started medbay, went into electrical, saw Charlie and then Alice come in from cafeteria. Charlie left toward security, and I stayed briefly on the electrical task, then I left back to medbay. Eve seeing me in medbay actually matches that \u2014 I wasn\u2019t in electrical anymore.\n\nSo from my side, the last person confirmed going *toward* electrical after I left is Eve. She says she found it, but that also means she was the next one there after seeing me in medbay. I\u2019m not saying hard accuse Eve yet, but Charlie instantly jumping to \u201cFrank absolutely killed\u201d feels way too confident when he wasn\u2019t there after tick 4.\n\nBob says he was left side and saw nobody, Diana was apparently in security/weapons side. I think we need Diana\u2019s exact timing, because right now this is either someone slipped in after I left, or Eve\u2019s report is not as clean as she\u2019s making it sound."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433328.760492, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can completely vouch for Charlie's timeline. I started in navigation, moved up to security, and then headed into weapons. I saw Charlie enter security from the electrical hallway at exactly tick 6, which perfectly matches the 2-tick travel time if he left electrical at tick 4 like he said. \n\nBecause Charlie's story is completely verified, that means his account of leaving Frank and Alice alone in electrical at tick 4 is also solid. Frank, you admit you were in electrical with Alice right after Charlie left. Eve saw you in medbay afterwards, which means you fled the scene before she got there and found the body. \n\nWith only one Duck in this game, all the evidence points directly to Frank. Charlie is cleared in my book, Bob was on the complete opposite side of the map, and Eve reporting the body right after seeing Frank run away makes sense. I'm voting for Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433343.1787846, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433359.3842309, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433370.2826712, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433400.5864532, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "You\u2019re all locking this way too fast off an assumption, not an actual witness.\n\nCharlie being in security at tick 6 only proves he left electrical when he says he did. It does **not** prove Alice died while I was there. I\u2019m telling you plainly: Alice was alive when I left electrical and went back to medbay. Eve seeing me in medbay supports that route.\n\nThe only person who claims to have gone into electrical after seeing me is Eve, and then she reports. That is exactly the self-report window. If Eve came storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical, she had the cleanest chance to walk in, kill, and report while pinning it on the last person seen nearby.\n\nIf you vote me here, you\u2019re voting on \u201cFrank was once in the room,\u201d not \u201cFrank was seen killing\u201d or \u201cbody was immediately found after he left.\u201d I think this is Eve using Charlie\u2019s earlier sighting to frame me. I\u2019m voting Eve."}}
